{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"05281643-6bb8-4b20-b517-b408229e6cb9","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Repaired the four modules to enforce all rate-limiter invariants using only the Python standard library:\n\n- **[models.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_28952_1795228701476_baseline/models.py)**:\n  - `as_decimal` converts `Decimal`, `int`, `str`, and `float` directly via `Decimal(str(value))` without float round-tripping, rejecting booleans, unsupported types, non-finite values, and negative values with `ValueError`.\n  - `BucketState.__post_init__` normalizes all fields to `Decimal` and enforces `capacity \u003e 0` and `tokens \u003c= capacity`.\n- **[bucket.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_28952_1795228701476_baseline/bucket.py)**:\n  - `TokenBucket` initializes `updated_at` via the injected `clock` callable and uses `self.clock` in `refill` and `consume` when `now` is omitted.\n  - `refill` computes exact `Decimal` arithmetic (`state.tokens + (now - state.updated_at) * state.refill_rate`), caps at `capacity`, and ignores backward timestamps.\n  - `consume` validates both `amount` (`\u003e 0`) and `now` before mutating state.\n- **[registry.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_28952_1795228701476_baseline/registry.py)**:\n  - Removed the shared mutable default dictionary in `BucketRegistry.__init__` and indexed buckets by `(tenant_id, name)`.\n- **[middleware.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_28952_1795228701476_baseline/middleware.py)**:\n  - `RateLimiter.consume` validates all amounts (`\u003e 0`), resolves all participating buckets, and aggregates repeated bucket names before mutating state.\n  - Samples `registry.clock()` once for non-empty requests, refills participating buckets at that instant, checks total availability across all requested buckets, and rolls back `tokens` and `updated_at` to exact pre-request snapshots on failure or exception.\n","duration_seconds":109.1539965,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":43295,"output_tokens":5213,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":192141,"total_tokens":48508}}}
